  "parts": [
    {
      "type": "choice",
      "prompt": "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{(2^3 \\cdot 4^2)^3}{8^4}$",
      "marks": 1,
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "content": "$2^{-1}$",
          "correct": false,
          "why": "A negative power means the denominator was bigger, but the numerator is $2^{21}$ and the denominator is only $2^{12}$. Check the order you subtracted the powers."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "content": "$2^{9}$",
          "correct": true,
          "why": "$(2^3 \\cdot 2^4)^3 = (2^7)^3 = 2^{21}$ and $8^4 = (2^3)^4 = 2^{12}$, so the answer is $2^{21-12} = 2^9$."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "content": "$2^{5}$",
          "correct": false,
          "why": "Check how you rewrote $4^2$. It is $(2^2)^2 = 2^4$, and the outer cube applies to both factors in the bracket."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "content": "$2^{0}$",
          "correct": false,
          "why": "A power of $0$ would mean the numerator and denominator are equal. Write both as powers of $2$ and compare them."
        }
      ],
      "hint": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Write $4$ and $8$ as powers of $2$ before doing anything else." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Write every base as a power of $2$: $4^2 = 2^4$ and $8^4 = 2^{12}$." },
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Numerator: $(2^3 \\cdot 2^4)^3 = (2^7)^3 = 2^{21}$." },
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "So $\\dfrac{2^{21}}{2^{12}} = 2^{9}$." }
      ]
    }
  ],
